  description: Electronic speed controller for motor 2. Converts the flight controller's
    throttle signal into three-phase drive. In this simulation the ESC is modelled
    only as the first-order lag between a commanded and an actual rotor speed, which
    is the behaviour that affects flight.
  engineeringNotes: '[UNVERIFIED - FLIGHT SAFETY RELEVANT] The brief specifies 40
    A ESCs but does not state their voltage rating. A 6S pack is 25.2 V fully charged,
    and many 40 A ESCs are rated only to 4S. Confirm the ESCs are rated for 6S before
    connecting the pack. See Docs/10-UAV-Hardware-Layout.md.'
  explodeDirection: {x: -0.70710677, y: 0, z: -0.70710677}
  explodeDistanceM: 0.12
