  description: Supports the aircraft on the ground and holds the battery and camera
    clear of the surface. The footprint width is what determines how much slope the
    aircraft can be armed on without tipping onto its propellers.
  engineeringNotes: '[ESTIMATE] Geometry and mass are estimates. Gear compliance
    and touchdown energy absorption are not modelled: contact is handled by the single
    hull collider, so a hard landing does not deform anything.'
  explodeDirection: {x: 0.70710677, y: -2, z: -0.70710677}
  explodeDistanceM: 0.12
